": false, "isUserVerified": true, "text": "The stunning wall paintings have been dated as 1527 when the large timber framed hall house was new. A second storey was added later and the house converted into small 2 up 2 down cottages; the paintings were covered in whitewash below, and linen and wallpaper above. This cottage is privately owned and only open twice a year to the public (including Heritage Day). The owners have conserved and continue to maintain, happily for us, these important paintings.", "pinnedPriority": 0, "currentStatusId": 2}, "blobStorageUrl": null, "mediaTypeId": 1, "commentId": 839368, "filename": "7ca1ba83-7ec5-4b28-ab04-dfb3bad47e50.jpg", "url": "https://historicengland.org.uk/etl/1342208/7ca1ba83-7ec5-4b28-ab04-dfb3bad47e50.jpg", "starred": false, "description": null, "caption": "Nos 134 and 136"}, {"id": 1301113, "comment": {"id": 839368, "parentId": null, "userId": "0e8bdee4-c6ba-4f44-97b7-9f23b35f7013", "username": "Ros Mitton", "userAvatarUrl": "https://account.historicengland.org.uk/image/get/genericavatar", "email": null, "itemId": 323591, "externalId": null, "memberId": "326613", "numberOfContributions": 0, "isLoggedInUsersComment": false, "created": "2026-09-16T17:25:12.8389193", "lastEdited": "2026-09-16T17:25:12.8389193", "isCreatedByOrganisationUser": false, "edited": false, "isUserVerified": true, "text": "The stunning wall paintings have been dated as 1527 when the large timber framed hall house was new. A second storey was added later and the house converted into small 2 up 2 down cottages; the paintings were covered in whitewash below, and linen and wallpaper above. This cottage is privately owned and only open twice a year to the public (including Heritage Day). The owners have conserved and continue to maintain, happily for us, these important paintings.", "pinnedPriority": 0, "currentStatusId": 2}, "blobStorageUrl": null, "mediaTypeId": 1, "commentId": 839368, "filename": "a404a0df-4efe-4f8b-bd80-ecf6c85c9b79.jpg", "url": "h